volume, you're going to get a different balance in the distribution.

512
00:31:51,964 --> 00:31:53,982
The key points to highlight before we finish,

513
00:31:53,982 --> 00:31:55,748
and hopefully you can make your mind

514
00:31:55,748 --> 00:31:57,261
up about this, is the follows.

515
00:31:57,964 --> 00:32:01,764
Where was price accepted? That's the most important thing to understand.

516
00:32:01,864 --> 00:32:06,227
The whole point of using profiles is to determine where

517
00:32:06,227 --> 00:32:08,408
is price being accepted and

518
00:32:08,408 --> 00:32:11,462
then secondly, where is price being rejected?

519
00:32:11,964 --> 00:32:18,764
If you can answer these two questions, it doesn't really matter whether you use traditional valuers or normal volume-based valuers.

520
00:32:19,064 --> 00:32:24,764
The question is, where is the market accepting price and where is the market rejecting price?

521
00:32:26,868 --> 00:32:29,322
We're going to conclude part three

522
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:31,776
now and talk about four basic

523
00:32:31,776 --> 00:32:34,230
important principles you're going to see

524
00:32:34,230 --> 00:32:35,866
in volume distribution profiling.

525
00:32:36,768 --> 00:32:42,368
They are fair value, discount, premium and exuberant prices.

526
00:32:42,968 --> 00:32:45,168
So first and foremost, fair value.

527
00:32:45,868 --> 00:32:50,968
Fair value is the point at which buyers and sellers agree to a certain price.

528
00:32:51,568 --> 00:32:58,268
These are price levels that are attracting the greatest volume or trade over various time frames.

529
00:32:58,768 --> 00:33:01,253
When fair value is established, it

530
00:33:01,253 --> 00:33:03,738
will require a change in fundamentals

531
00:33:03,738 --> 00:33:07,466
or perception to move beyond what was deemed fair.

532
00:33:08,068 --> 00:33:14,268
By that token, once fair value is established, the market spends time within the price boundaries of fair value.

533
00:33:14,868 --> 00:33:22,168
This is the price where an area in which 70% of all trade, whether that's time or volume, is being accepted.

534
00:33:22,768 --> 00:33:28,568
So in essence, what is fair value? It's merely the point where buyers and sellers agree with one another.

535
00:33:28,968 --> 00:33:30,468
How do we move out of fair value?

536
00:33:30,768 --> 00:33:37,068
Well, it requires a very big shift in perception or fundamentals to move us away from fair value.

537
00:33:37,468 --> 00:33:41,768
So by that token, markets spend a long, long time within fair value.

538
00:33:42,668 --> 00:33:44,068
What's the next principle?

539
00:33:45,568 --> 00:33:46,568
Discount prices.

540
00:33:47,068 --> 00:33:49,560
As the name suggests, a discount price is

541
00:33:49,560 --> 00:33:52,052
the price at which a buyer aggressively enters

542
00:33:52,052 --> 00:33:55,167
the market in order to capture a price being advertised.

543
00:33:55,768 --> 00:33:58,268
at a lower price than perceived fair value.

544
00:33:58,768 --> 00:34:01,476
Markets will very quickly move away from

545
00:34:01,476 --> 00:34:04,184
discounted prices and often these are depicted

546
00:34:04,184 --> 00:34:07,666
with tails or very aggressive buy side price action.

547
00:34:08,568 --> 00:34:15,868
Once a market has determined a certain price as a discount, the price becomes a pivotal area for future reference.

548
00:34:16,368 --> 00:34:22,968
In essence, if something's cheap, buyers are going to step in very aggressively to take advantage of it being cheap.

549
00:34:23,568 --> 00:34:25,868
Now what is cheap? Well it's a matter of perception.

550
00:34:26,368 --> 00:34:29,468
So we don't just assume that any price is cheap,

551
00:34:29,468 --> 00:34:31,948
we allow the market to tell us based

552
00:34:31,948 --> 00:34:35,668
on its response that there is a discount and then we respond.

553
00:34:36,968 --> 00:34:42,868
Do note, fair value does not equal market value. A lot of people make this mistake.

554
00:34:43,168 --> 00:34:47,468
Just because a market is accepting prices doesn't mean that is fair value.

555
00:34:48,968 --> 00:34:51,994
Just because a market accepts something as the market value

556
00:34:51,994 --> 00:34:54,415
doesn't mean it's fair value, which means we

557
00:34:54,415 --> 00:34:56,836
can, for a long, long time, move up

558
00:34:56,836 --> 00:35:00,467
and down away from prices trying to establish where fair value is.

559
00:35:02,912 --> 00:35:05,012
The next principle we're going to discuss is premium.

560
00:35:06,212 --> 00:35:08,571
Premium is the prices at which sellers

561
00:35:08,571 --> 00:35:11,267
aggressively enter the market in order to capture

562
00:35:11,267 --> 00:35:15,311
a price being advertised at a higher price than perceived fair value.

563
00:35:15,812 --> 00:35:18,612
Markets will very quickly move away from

564
00:35:18,612 --> 00:35:21,412
premium prices and often these are depicted

565
00:35:21,412 --> 00:35:24,612
with tails or very aggressive sell-side price action.

566
00:35:25,112 --> 00:35:32,512
Once a market has determined a certain price as premium, the price becomes a pivotal area for future reference.

567
00:35:32,812 --> 00:35:37,374
So again, just like discounted prices where buyers enter aggressively

568
00:35:37,374 --> 00:35:41,024
to pick up those prices and the advantage,

569
00:35:41,024 --> 00:35:47,411
sellers enter when prices enter a premium or an area known as premium prices.

570
00:35:48,512 --> 00:35:51,933
Now note, the key thing in both discount and premium

571
00:35:51,933 --> 00:35:55,011
prices worth mentioning is that the point at which

572
00:35:55,011 --> 00:35:57,747
a price is deemed a discount or premium,

573
00:35:57,747 --> 00:36:01,510
in the future that price point becomes a key pivot point.

574
00:36:01,812 --> 00:36:04,889
And we will discuss this at a later stage when talking about

575
00:36:04,889 --> 00:36:06,940
strategy, but this is something you definitely want

576
00:36:06,940 --> 00:36:07,709
to watch out.

577
00:36:07,912 --> 00:36:13,712
These reference points often act as very good areas for momentum type strategies.

578
00:36:15,112 --> 00:36:19,412
The last principle we want to talk about is excess or exuberant prices.

579
00:36:20,412 --> 00:36:24,612
When the auction process extends beyond prices of fair value

580
00:36:24,612 --> 00:36:27,132
as well as discount and premium

581
00:36:27,132 --> 00:36:30,912
prices, we then enter excess prices or exuberant prices.

582
00:36:31,612 --> 00:36:36,912
The reasoning behind these prices being advertised stem from the psychology behind buyers and sellers.

583
00:36:37,712 --> 00:36:44,054
Volatility and panic can force participants to lose sight of what is fair, and as such

584
00:36:44,054 --> 00:36:48,811
markets can advertise at prices which would under normal circumstances seem illogical.

585
00:36:49,612 --> 00:36:53,012
These are deemed excess or exuberant prices.

586
00:36:53,512 --> 00:36:58,212
Whilst these prices can often be reversed relatively fast, timing is essential.

587
00:36:59,012 --> 00:37:03,212
As markets can remain illogical a lot longer than investors remaining liquid.

588
00:37:03,912 --> 00:37:06,867
The key point to note is once a

589
00:37:06,867 --> 00:37:10,561
market finds an excess top or bottom, these tend to

590
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:17,211
hold as highs and lows for longer periods as the market begins a process of balancing and stability.

591
00:37:17,712 --> 00:37:19,704
So note, when you find a

592
00:37:19,704 --> 00:37:22,360
